      "eli5": {
        "text": "When an automated step in the system hits an error, the error message now gets saved into the running conversation's history so it becomes part of the context the assistant has when it tries again or is debugged. This only affects the backend orchestration of programmatic steps today; no end-user behavior changes yet because nothing reads that stored error history. The assistant itself doesn't visibly speak the error to you now; this is purely behind-the-scenes record-keeping for developers chasing down failures of automated step execution.",
